  "question": {
    "text": "A tower <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> of height <math><mn>60</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>m</mi></math> is located exactly opposite to a tower <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> of height <math><mn>80</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>m</mi></math> on a straight road. From the top of <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> if the angle of depression of the foot of <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is twice the angle of elevation of the top of <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> then the width (in <math><mi>m</mi></math>) of the road between the feet of the towers <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
